  "PublishCopy": {
    "title": "& used to be the 27th letter of the alphabet",
    "description": "See this squiggle? The and sign. It used to be the 27th letter of the alphabet.\nThe & is the Latin word et, its E and T joined in Roman handwriting. Children recited it after Z as 'and per se and', which slurred into 'ampersand'. And no, it isn't named after Ampère.",
